        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5ded8a73-8c3e-56c1-a392-3091b4929926",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Hong Kong, Diamond Hill, Lantau Island, Ngong Ping\n- Organizations: Chi Lin Nunnery, Po Lin Monastery\n- Products: Tian Tan Buddha, Big Buddha\n- Concepts: Buddhist temples, Tang Dynasty architectural style\n\nFacts:\n- Chi Lin Nunnery in Diamond Hill is one of the most prominent Buddhist temples in Hong Kong and was built in the Tang Dynasty architectural style.\n- Tian Tan Buddha is a large bronze statue of Buddha Shakyamuni located at Ngong Ping on Lantau Island in Hong Kong.\n- Tian Tan Buddha is also known as the Big Buddha and was completed in 1993.\n- Po Lin Monastery on Lantau Island is one of the most prominent Buddhist temples in Hong Kong and is famous for the outdoor bronze statue Tian Tan Buddha.\n- Tian Tan Buddha attracts large numbers of visitors during weekends and holidays.",
